        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for your kind words!\r\n\r\nAs for the features:\r\n1. My initial reaction was \"Not really possible with current design\". But after some digging, I think I found a reasonable implementation for this. I'll try and update in a couple of days.\r\n2. Every custom highlighting in this package is done with corresponding highlight group. All highlighted groups defined within module are listed in its \"# Highlight groups\" section of help file. A dedicated mechanism to change highlighting to your liking is update the highlight group with [`highlight`](https://vimhelp.org/syntax.txt.html#%3Ahighlight) command. In your case it will be `hi! link MiniCursorword Visual`. Put this in your init file after loading colorscheme and this module.",
