            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This is very strange. I tried it with both very minimal setup (only `mini.nvim` plugin and `mini.cursorword` with highlight groups) and my main one. Both times it works as expected. If I could look at your setup, it would be easier, but they don't seem to be public.\r\n\r\nLet's be methodical here. Are you sure that you are using the latest version of `mini.nvim`? For example, have you run `PackerSync` if you use `packer.nvim`? To be 100% sure, could you please find where you installed `mini.nvim` (it should be present as entry in `:echo &runtimepath`) and look if [this line](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/lua/mini/cursorword.lua#L80) is present.\r\n\r\n**Edit**: If this proved to be true, could you, please, post the output of `:echo getmatches()` executed at the time, when you would expect it to highlight words.",
