        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "At the moment I tend to work without strict rules and backlog but something like this:\r\n- Main work branch is `main`. All new features and bug fixes will go there after my initial alpha-testing.\r\n- After there are \"enough\" of changes, I'll make new release and update `stable` branch. You'll see that something moved to `stable` by many new commits merged to it.\r\n\r\nThis is somewhat similar to the situation with Neovim nightly and new Neovim release.",
